== how much of the LoRA delta a bf16 output keeps (applied delta = out - W against the LoRA's B A, fp32)
moss_realism_v1: 164 modules, |BA| / |W| median 1.77e-03; cosine(applied, BA) min 0.640 median 0.800; |applied| / |BA| median 0.981
moss_image_sft_4step_v2.0: 168 modules, |BA| / |W| median 3.40e-04; cosine(applied, BA) min 0.267 median 0.452; |applied| / |BA| median 0.594
   bf16 has 8 mantissa bits: a delta far below the weight's step is rounded away or rounded to a full step, so the applied delta is a noisy version of B A. Bake small or few step LoRAs to fp32 (--format fp32), or keep them as LoRAs.
